        page["content"] = "`f64(value)` is Capy's f64 constructor for a `dval`. `f64(value, fallback)` returns the fallback for `none` or a failed conversion.\n\nExact numeric strings, finite f64 values, and booleans can convert. Empty, invalid, and non-finite strings return the fallback. Maps and lists also return the fallback.\n\n## C++ API\n\n`DValue::to_f64()` also converts C++ pointers, resolved references, and one-child maps. These C++ rules do not change the Capy constructor rules.\n"
        page["returns"] = "converted value or the fallback"
