        page["route"] = "/doc/api/dvalue-to-s64/"
        page["title"] = "DValue::to_s64"
        page["content"] = "`s64(value)` is Capy's signed integer constructor for a `dval`. `s64(value, fallback)` returns the fallback for `none` or a failed conversion. `s32(value)` uses the same rules with the s32 range and a default fallback of `0`.\n\nExact decimal strings, in-range finite f64 values, and booleans can convert. An f64 conversion truncates toward zero. Empty or invalid strings, overflow, maps, and lists return the fallback.\n\n## C++ API\n\n`DValue::to_s64()` also converts C++ pointers, resolved references, and one-child maps. It can clamp values outside its range. These C++ rules do not change the Capy constructor rules.\n"
