        page["title"] = "DValue::to_string"
        page["content"] = "`string(value)` is Capy's string constructor for a `dval`. `string(value, fallback)` returns the fallback for `none` or a failed conversion.\n\nIt returns stored text, f64 text, and boolean text. Capy boolean text is `true` or `false`.\n\nAn empty string, a map, or an unsupported value returns the fallback. Ordinary `print(value.member)` uses `as string` and has the same conversion.\n\n## C++ API\n\n`DValue::to_string()` also converts pointers. It returns the fallback for an unresolved reference or an unknown type.\n\nC++ `DValue::to_string()` returns `(true)` or `(false)` for boolean values. This differs from Capy boolean text.\n"
        page["returns"] = "converted value or the fallback"
